{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788116214,"nonce":"foUGW09lRsuFItjV46pePzeqy90=","message":"AMENDMENT from spike 0.1 (FINDINGS.md, git-bug 3fa4cf5) — orchestrator, post-gate.\n\nTwo bench facts that shape the digest. Scope and Acceptance stand.\n\n**Alerts trail the tick that caused them.** Alerts are recomputed by\n`UIRootUpdate` on its own cadence, not per tick, so under fast-forward the\nreadout reflects state from a frame or two ago. Since this spec takes alert\nlabels verbatim from AlertsReadout (the right call — it IS the attention model),\nthe digest's alert list is a trailing signal by construction. DESIGN already\nsays alerts fire late by design; this adds that they are additionally late by a\nframe under advance. Worth one line in the field docs so 5.1 does not write an\nassertion that assumes tick-exactness.\n\n**The default bench colony is small and hostile.** `-quicktest`\n(`Root_Play.SetupForQuickTestPlay`) gives Crashlanded, Cassandra **Rough**, 0.3\nplanet coverage, 250x250 map, random seed — 3 colonists. That is the shape the\n1-2KB budget must hold for, and it is what the spike measured against. Note\nthat a fresh quicktest costs 2-4 min of worldgen per boot; for repeatable\ndigest fixtures prefer the `autostart.rws` path (with devMode on, a save of\nthat name auto-loads on entering the Play scene, per\n`SaveGameFilesUtility.GetAutostartSaveFile`) — no UI, no worldgen.\n\n**Bench modlist is larger than DESIGN's list.** 38 active: 6 DLC + 32 mods,\nincluding Hospitality/Gastronomy/Storefront/CashRegister and Guests +\nRegisterLanes. So the digest will meet modded alerts, modded rooms and guest\npawns from day one, not eventually. Relevant to the \"what makes the cut at\nbudget\" open question: guests and visitors are already present on the bench.","files":null}]}